    "extracted text": "The paper investigates Al-Cu 206 cast alloys with varying Fe, Mn, and Si content to evaluate the effect of iron-rich intermetallics on tensile properties. The alloys are designated using a three-digit system where the first digit stands for the approximate content of Fe (B for baseline at max 0.15% Fe), and the second and third digits stand for Si and Mn contents respectively. All alloys underwent T4 (solution treatment and natural aging) and T7 (solution treatment and artificial overaging) heat treatments. The solution treatment was performed at 505°C for 2 hours, followed by 520°C for 8 hours, then water quenching to room temperature. For T4, samples were naturally aged at room temperature for at least 7 days. For T7, samples were artificially aged at 185°C for 5 hours.",
    "property mapping": "UTS (MPa) = Ultimate Tensile Strength in megapascals\nYS (MPa) = Yield Strength at 0.2% offset strain in megapascals\nEl (pct) = Elongation percentage\nT4 = Solution treatment and natural aging\nT7 = Solution treatment and artificial overaging",
    "abbreviations": "B11, B33, 311, 333, 511, 515, 533 - Alloy designations where the first digit stands for the approximate content of Fe (B for baseline at a maximum specification limit of 0.15% Fe), and the second and third digits stand for Si and Mn contents respectively.\nbal = balance (remainder of composition is aluminum)\nT4 = Solution treatment followed by natural aging at room temperature\nT7 = Solution treatment followed by artificial overaging at 185°C for 5 hours\nUTS = Ultimate Tensile Strength\nYS = Yield Strength\nEl = Elongation",
